
Now let's learn Normalization, which is all about designing databases properly.

What is Normalization?

Normalization is the process of organizing data to:

✅ Reduce duplicate data
✅ Avoid data inconsistency
✅ Improve database design

Why Do We Need Normalization?

Imagine this table:

student_id	student_name	course1	course2
1	Nanda	SQL	Java
2	Ravi	Python	NULL

Problems:

Multiple courses in one row
Difficult to add more courses
Wastes space

This is a bad design.

First Normal Form (1NF)
Rule:

Each cell must contain only ONE value.

❌ Not 1NF

student_id	name	courses
1	Nanda	SQL, Java

Because one cell contains multiple values.

✅ 1NF

student_id	name	course
1	Nanda	SQL
1	Nanda	Java

Now every cell contains only one value.

Second Normal Form (2NF)
Rule:
Must already be in 1NF
Remove partial dependency

Consider:

student_id	course_id	student_name	course_name
1	101	Nanda	SQL
2	102	Ravi	Java

Problem:

student_name depends only on student_id
course_name depends only on course_id

They don't depend on the entire key.

Solution

Split into two tables.

Students
student_id	student_name
1	Nanda
2	Ravi
Courses
course_id	course_name
101	SQL
102	Java
Third Normal Form (3NF)
Rule:
Must be in 2NF
Remove transitive dependency

Example:

emp_id	emp_name	dept_id	dept_name
1	John	10	HR
2	Jane	20	IT

Problem:

emp_id → dept_id
dept_id → dept_name

So:

emp_id indirectly determines dept_name

This is called transitive dependency.

Solution

Split tables.

Employees
emp_id	emp_name	dept_id
1	John	10
2	Jane	20
Departments
dept_id	dept_name
10	HR
20	IT
Visual Summary
Unnormalized Data
        ↓
1NF
(Atomic Values)
        ↓
2NF
(Remove Partial Dependency)
        ↓
3NF
(Remove Transitive Dependency)
Easy Interview Definitions
1NF

Each column contains atomic (single) values.

2NF

Remove partial dependency.

3NF

Remove transitive dependency.

Real World Example (Event Planner App)

Instead of:

user_id	user_name	event_name	venue_name

Create:

Users

| user_id | user_name |

Events

| event_id | event_name |

Venues

| venue_id | venue_name |

Bookings

| booking_id | user_id | event_id |

This is a normalized design.

